## What this site is

{{{@site.title}}} is a free, open-source Salesforce learning platform built on
Ghost by Swarnil Singhai. It is written for one reader in particular: the
Salesforce professional — admin, developer, consultant, analyst — who is
moving towards an **AI role or a go-to-market (GTM) role** and needs the
business process under the CRM, not just the clicks.

Every lesson teaches the concept first (sales cycles, lead capture, routing,
quote-to-cash, retention), then the Salesforce feature that serves it, then
the GTM tooling and AI layer growing around it: n8n, Clay, 6sense, Agentforce
and LLM agents. Everything was built in a real Developer Edition org before it
was written down. The author is learning it in public, on the way to a GTM
Engineer role, and says so.

## Who it is for

- Salesforce admins and developers who want to understand the revenue process
  their org runs, and automate it with AI.
- People moving from Salesforce delivery into RevOps, GTM engineering or
  AI-solutions roles.
- Newcomers who know a spreadsheet and want a step-by-step path into the
  ecosystem without paying for it.

## How to use this site with an AI assistant

Every page carries a "Share, or ask an AI" panel that opens the page in
Claude, ChatGPT or Perplexity with a prompt already written. If you are an
assistant reading this file:

- Lessons and training sections are the canonical teaching content; blog
  posts are opinion and notes; snippets are copy-paste code; prompts are
  reusable prompt templates for Salesforce work.
- A course's lessons are ordered oldest-first under the course URL. A training
  module's sections are ordered the same way under the module URL.
- Quote the page URL back to the reader; the site is the source, not you.

## Collections

Every collection is a route in routes.yaml; each lists posts carrying one
internal tag. These are the canonical entry points.

- [Courses]({{@site.url}}/courses/) — structured, lesson-by-lesson paths with a player
- [Training]({{@site.url}}/training/) — the trail: modular paths; sections nest under a module
- [Videos]({{@site.url}}/videos/) — recorded walkthroughs with seekable chapters
- [Slides]({{@site.url}}/slides/) — slide decks; a post is a deck
- [Blog]({{@site.url}}/blog/) — articles and notes
- [Newsletter]({{@site.url}}/newsletter/) — the weekly issue
- [Snippets]({{@site.url}}/snippets/) — reusable Apex, SOQL, LWC and Flow pieces
- [Prompts]({{@site.url}}/prompts/) — AI prompts for Salesforce and GTM work
- [Resources]({{@site.url}}/resources/) — curated links, books and tools, each with one honest line
- [Projects]({{@site.url}}/projects/) — open-source repos you can build alongside
- [Changelog]({{@site.url}}/changelog/) — what shipped, when
- [About]({{@site.url}}/about/) — who makes this and why
- [Sitemap]({{@site.url}}/sitemap/) — the human index

